  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hiralal Uttam Patil vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 29 July, 2024 Author: Shivkumar Dige Bench: Shivkumar Dige 2024:Bhc-Aug:16094 1 595. In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay, Bench At Aurangabad. 58 Anticipatory Bail Application No. 595 Of 2024 Hiralal Uttam Patil Versus The State Of Maharashtra And Another ... Advocate for Applicant : Mr. Patil Jitendra Vijay App for Respondent/State : Ms.V.S. Chaudhari ... Coram : Shivkumar Dige, J. Date : 29th July, 2024. P.C.: 1. The applicant easily ran away in presence of police from the incident spot.",
    "facts": "The applicant apprehends arrest in connection with F.I.R. No.111 of 2024 registered with Midc Police Station, Jalgaon, for the offences punishable under sections 328, 188, 272, 273 of the Indian Penal Code (For short, \"Ipc\") and sections 26 and 27 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. It is alleged that when the police inquired with the applicant about the said Gutkha, he ran away from the incident spot when the police were loading the seized Gutkha Hiralal Uttam Patil vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 29 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/196969736/ 1 in the vehicle. 3. Considering the allegations against the applicant, the custodial interrogation of the applicant is not required, hence requested to allow the application.",
    "arguments": "It is the contention of the learned counsel for the applicant that the applicant has been falsely implicated in this case."
  },
